    "body": "Replace the inline BlockStored(...) in cache_partial_block with a call to _build_block_stored_event, consistent with cache_full_blocks and emit_cached_block_events. Update the method's docstring to reflect all three callers.\r\n\r\n## Purpose\r\n`cache_partial_block` was constructing `BlockStored` events inline, duplicating the fields already centralized in `_build_block_stored_event` (token_ids slice, lora_id/lora_name, medium, session_id). This is inconsistent with `cache_full_blocks` and `emit_cached_block_events`, which both use that helper.\r\n\r\nThis PR replaces the inline construction in `cache_partial_block` with a call to `_build_block_stored_event`, and updates the method's docstring to reflect all three callers: the two write paths (`cache_full_blocks`, `cache_partial_block`) and the cache-hit path (`emit_cached_block_events`).\r\n\r\n## Test Plan\r\npytest tests/v1/core/test_prefix_caching.py --noconftest -q -k \"not hisparse_async\"\r\n\r\n## Test Result\r\n145 passed, 5 deselected, 1 warning in 6.27s",
